<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <!-- Assembly name is the invoked command, so help usage and the MCP server name read "slnmap". -->
    <AssemblyName>slnmap</AssemblyName>
    <Description>Slnmap (sln-map) — a semantic map of your .sln for AI coding agents. Analyze a .NET solution into a queryable code graph, serve it over MCP, and inspect index status.</Description>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>slnmap</ToolCommandName>
    <PackageId>Slnmap</PackageId>
    <Version>0.13.0</Version>
    <RollForward>Major</RollForward>
    <PackageReadmeFile>nuget-readme.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Authors>Mahmoud Nabil</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Mahmoud Nabil</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://slnmap.dev</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/EMahmoudNabil/slnmap</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageTags>dotnet;roslyn;mcp;ai;code-analysis;claude-code;knowledge-graph</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Fix (slnmap-ts 0.3.0): a verb-named call through a locally-declared
wrapper function was always reported unrecognized-callee, even when the wrapper cleanly
forwarded its own parameter into a real HTTP client call one level down (a "requests.get calls
superagent.get" wrapper shape) -- the dominant real-world pattern for any non-toy React
codebase. Confirmed against a real open-source frontend: 0/22 call sites resolved before this
fix, 22/22 after. Traces exactly one level of such indirection, only when provably safe
(const-rooted, a single clean forwarding expression, the parameter provably referenced in the
inner call's URL argument); anything less clear-cut still falls back to the existing disclosed
unrecognized-callee, never a guess.
Fix (slnmap-ts 0.3.0): a wrapper's own internal HTTP-client call was independently
double-counted as a spurious second call site -- found while building the fix above; fixed with
an upfront discovery pass that excludes confirmed wrapper-internal calls from independent
classification.
Fix: the cross-stack linker never recognized an absolute-URL call-site template (an API_ROOT-
style base URL, resolvable at all only once the slnmap-ts fix above lands), so it could never
link to a relative backend endpoint -- the linker collapsed a leading double-slash but never
stripped the scheme and host ahead of it, leaving a segment-count mismatch that always rejects.
Fixed: the scheme and host are cleanly separated from the path before matching, anchored to
strings that actually start with a scheme, so an ordinary relative call site carrying an
embedded URL inside its own query string is unaffected. An absolute-URL call site is now
matched by path only; a host that can't be cleanly isolated is disclosed rather than guessed at
either way.
Added: CallSiteLinkResult now carries Host -- populated whenever a call site's template is an
absolute URL, regardless of link outcome, so a call site to a genuinely different, external API
still links by path but stays visibly external rather than silently hidden. See CHANGELOG.md
for details.
Source: https://github.com/EMahmoudNabil/slnmap</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\docs\nuget-readme.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\viz-template.html" LogicalName="viz-template.html" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\vis-network.min.js" LogicalName="vis-network.min.js" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Analysis\Slnmap.Analysis.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Core\Slnmap.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Mcp\Slnmap.Mcp.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Storage\Slnmap.Storage.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.CommandLine" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Slnmap.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
